well a hidden gem here in the valley  catches fire now the owners really need  some help to bring it back  mema's kitchen is over on charleston in  commerce they're known for colombian and  mexican dishes  it was destroyed last week sally  jeremiah shares their story mimas  was a food truck that we started about  two years ago with my family carlos  arturo monsalve castro along with his  uncle juan riven on  marieli diaz are from bucaramanga  colombia and realized las vegas needed a  fast food colombian concept  the sachi papa were like loaded hot  loaded fries as well too  fried plantains with toppings on top  from empanadas  to hot dogs and burgers they served it  all my uncle is miguel  my auntis maya so that's why mima's is  the name of mimas right there even  reinventing themselves this past year  offering a fusion of colombian and  mexican plates it was a way for  my family to share some of our  traditions and our food and our flavors  but then the worst imaginable happen  unfortunately there seemed to have been  an electrical issue  that started after hours and that turned  into  a fire we got a call from the tire shop  that  was right next to our our food truck and  so we went there and we tried to  extinguish the pie or the fire  extinguisher but  everything was pretty much burned down  shuttering their business they worked so  hard to build people reaching out and  asking  you know what happened and asking when  we're going to be open up again so we  can serve them and now many loyal  customers in las vegas  want this corner to come back to life  we're still trying to figure out how we  can  make mimas come back better and stronger  than before we all as a family  have for all the community is simply  thank you  sally jaramillo 8 news now mima's  kitchen is a total loss they're hoping  to raise ten thousand dollars to get  back in business so far they have raised  four thousand  now we shared their story and gofundme  it's over on eightnewsnow.com
 

